<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head><meta charset='utf-8'><title>FL2024- exam 30</title>
<style>
body { font-family: Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; }
h1 { color: #C0392B; font-size: 20pt; }
h2 { color: #1F618D; font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 24px; }
.qtext { font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 8px; white-space: pre-wrap; }
.opt { margin: 4px 0 4px 20px; }
.correct { color: green; font-weight: bold; }
.selectedwrong { color: red; font-weight: bold; }
.selectedright { color: green; font-weight: bold; }
.explain { background: #F4F6F6; padding: 8px; margin-top: 8px; font-style: italic; }
.video { margin-top:6px; }
img { max-width: 500px; margin: 10px 0; display:block; }
</style></head><body><h1>FL2024- EXAM 30 - Ket qua &amp; giai thich</h1><p><b>Ho ten:</b> Hang Tran<br/><b>Ket qua:</b> 7/40<br/><b>Thoi gian lam bai:</b> 56 giây<br/><b>Nop bai:</b> 2026-08-03T08:48:25.928Z</p><hr/><h2>Cau hoi 1</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following BEST describes a tester participating in a retrospective meeting?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. As a tester participating in a retrospective meeting, I should bring in topics that are related to testing only. All other topics will be covered by different participants [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. As a tester, I participate in a retrospective meeting as an observer, ensuring that the meeting follows the retrospective rules and agile values</div><div class="opt correct">c. As a tester participating in a retrospective meeting, I should provide feedback and input on all activities conducted by the team during the sprint [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. As a tester, I should only attend and participate in a retrospective meeting if I have any feedback and input related to activities conducted by the team during the sprint</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.1.6. Retrospective meeting. Tester nên tham gia vào tất cả các hoạt động của dự án để giúp cải tiến quy trình của dự án vì thế nên loại A vì "I should bring in topics that are related to testing only" Loại B vì "as an observer- ý là người quan sát ko đóng góp ý kiến gì, Loại D vì " I should only attend and participate in a retrospective meeting if I have any feedback - Chỉ tham gia vào meeting nếu có phản hồi, nếu ko có thì ko tham gia " là sai.</div><h2>Cau hoi 2</h2><div class="qtext">Debugging and testing are different. Dynamic testing can show failures that are cause by defects. Debugging is the development activity that find, analyzes and removes the cause of failure. Which of following is the example of debuging?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A tester retests a fix from a developer and finds a regression [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. A developer performs unit test</div><div class="opt ">c. A tester finds defect and reports its</div><div class="opt correct">d. A developer finds and fixes a defect [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 1.1.2</div><h2>Cau hoi 3</h2><div class="qtext">The most visible part of testing i test execution. But to be effective and efficient, test plan should also include time to be spent on planning the tests, designing test cases, preparing for execution and evaluating result. Which of following is a major task of test planning?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Determining the test approach [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Preparing test specifications</div><div class="opt ">c. Evaluating exit criteria and reporting</div><div class="opt ">d. Measuring and analyzing results</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 1.4 , B là của test design, D là của monitoring và C là của control</div><h2>Cau hoi 4</h2><div class="qtext">Which of following statement does NOT define the level of independence from low to high? i. Test designed by a person from an independent test team or performance test specialists ii. Test designed by a person from an outsourcing or certification by an external body iii. Test designed by the person who wrote the software under test with the low level of independence iv. Test designed by another person form development team</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. i, ii, iii, iv [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. iv, ii, i, iii</div><div class="opt ">c. iii, iv, i, ii</div><div class="opt ">d. iv, iii, ii, i</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 5.1. Ở câu này sắp xếp nào cũng sai, C thì là theo thứ tự đúng từ thấp đến cao nên ko phải là đáp án, còn 3 đáp án khác sắp xếp đều sai nhưng chọn A vì là sai nhất do i, ii là mức độc lập nhất lại để lên đầu</div><h2>Cau hoi 5</h2><div class="qtext">Which describes about the 'Tests wear out' is one of Seven Principles of Testing ?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Testing is done differently in different context. For example, safety-critical software is tested differently from an ecommerce site [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. If the same tests are repeated over and over again, no new defects can be found. To overcome this pesticide paradox, test cases need to be regularly reviewed and revised; new and different tests need to be written to exercise different parts of the software to find potentially more defects [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Test everything (all combination of inputs and preconditions) is not feasible. Instead of exhaustive testing, risk analysis and priorities should be used to focus testing efforts</div><div class="opt ">d. To find early defects, testing activities should start as early as possible in the software or software development life cycle and should focus on defined objectives</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 1.3. A là của nguyên lý 6.Testing is context dependent , B là của nguyên lý 5. Tests wear out, C là của 2. Exhaustive testing is impossible, D là của 3. Early testing saves time and money</div><h2>Cau hoi 6</h2><div class="qtext">Which is NOT part of the test process ?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Performing the test basis [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Logging test results</div><div class="opt ">c. Reviewing the test basis</div><div class="opt ">d. Verify test environment</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Chọn A vì nó là task của BA không phải của tester</div><h2>Cau hoi 7</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is NOT a principle of continuous integration?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Continuous integration helps to build changed software regularly, including testing and deploying, in an automated way [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Continuous integration allows new builds to be available frequently to testers and stakeholders</div><div class="opt ">c. Continuous integration helps to identify new integration defects early and makes the analysis of these defects easier</div><div class="opt correct">d. Continuous integration ensures that testing of builds is done manually, as this generates more reliable results than automated scripts [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 2.1.4. CI - Continuous integration là tích hợp liên tục thường xuyên và sớm có bản build để test sớm và tìm thấy lỗi sớm nên A, B, C đều đúng với CI, chỉ có D là đáp án của câu này vì "testing of builds is done manually" ý là test bản build manual thì tin cây hơn là script tự động ( sai hẳn so với 2.1.4 mô tả các phương pháp này đều đc thúc đẩy làm automated )</div><h2>Cau hoi 8</h2><div class="qtext">Which of following statement does NOT correctly describe a valid approach to Component testing?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Functional testing of the interfaces between modules [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Functional testing of the component in isolation</div><div class="opt ">c. Structure-based testing of the code without recording incidents</div><div class="opt ">d. Automation tests that are run until the component passes</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 2.2 chọn A vì the interfaces là của integration test</div><h2>Cau hoi 9</h2><div class="qtext">What are good practices for testing within the development life cycle?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Testers are involved in document reviews [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Different test levels are defined with specific objectives</div><div class="opt ">c. Early test analysis and design</div><div class="opt correct">d. All of above [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 2.1</div><h2>Cau hoi 10</h2><div class="qtext">Which of following is NOT the indicators of maintenance testing?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Retirement [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Creation [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Modification</div><div class="opt ">d. Migration</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 2.3 Triggers for Maintenance</div><h2>Cau hoi 11</h2><div class="qtext">Which testing is the repeated testing of an already tested program, after modification, to discover any defects introduced or uncovered as a result of changes?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Functional testing [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Non-functional testing</div><div class="opt ">c. Structure testing</div><div class="opt correct">d. Regression testing [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 2.3 để ý "to discover any defects introduced"</div><h2>Cau hoi 12</h2><div class="qtext">What is the purpose of performing regression testing when system maintenance activities have occurred?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. To ensure no unauthorized changes have been applied to the system [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. To assess the scope of maintenance performed on the system</div><div class="opt ">c. To identify any maintainability issues with the code</div><div class="opt correct">d. To ensure the overall system has not regressed [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 2.3 ta chọn D đảm bảo hệ thống không bị lỗi hồi quy. C sai vì maintainability, B là của impact analysis, A là hoạt động phê duyệt của con người</div><h2>Cau hoi 13</h2><div class="qtext">For which of following would a static analysis tool be useful?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Enforcement of coding standard [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Validating models of software</div><div class="opt ">c. Testing code executed in a special test harness</div><div class="opt ">d. Supporting reviews</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 3.1.3 static analysis tool tìm ra các lỗi liên quan đến code</div><h2>Cau hoi 14</h2><div class="qtext">Which testing technique would be most effective is determining and improving maintainability of the code?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Dynamic testing [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Unit testing</div><div class="opt ">c. Peer review</div><div class="opt correct">d. Static analysis [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 3.1.3</div><h2>Cau hoi 15</h2><div class="qtext">The followings details about main phases of a formal review, which is NOT correct?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Planning: defining the scope, purpose and quality characteristics to be evaluated [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Kick-off meeting: access to the work product under review, receives everything needed to perform the review</div><div class="opt correct">c. Rework: analyze and discusse all these anomalies at the physical meeting [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Follow up: checking that the exit criteria are reached</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 3.2.1 review process, các đáp án khác mô tả đúng, C đang mô tả cho Review meeting chứ ko phải Rework</div><h2>Cau hoi 16</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is NOT the one of Experience-based techniques?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Error guessing [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Exploratory testing</div><div class="opt ">c. Checklist based testing</div><div class="opt correct">d. Cause Effect Graphing [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 4.4. chọn D vì là của black box test ( advanced sẽ dạy)</div><h2>Cau hoi 17</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following statements for the boundary value test technique is TRUE?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Is the same as equivalence partitioning tests [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Is used in white box testing strategy</div><div class="opt ">c. Test combinations of input circumstances</div><div class="opt correct">d. Test boundary conditions on, below and above the edges of input and output equivalence class [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 4.2.2 Boundary value analysis (BVA) - Test at the edge of each equivalence partition - Two-point boundary: The maximum and minimum values - Three- point boundary: Before, at, over</div><h2>Cau hoi 18</h2><div class="qtext">If you are testing a module of code, how do you determine the level of decision coverage you have achieved?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. By taking the number of decisions you have tested and dividing that by the total number of executable statements in the module [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. By taking the number of decisions you have tested and dividing that by the total number of decisions in the module</div><div class="opt ">c. By taking the number of decisions you have tested and dividing that by the total lines of code in the module</div><div class="opt correct">d. By taking the number of decision outcomes you have tested and dividing that by the total number of decision outcomes in the module [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 4.3.2 Decision coverage/ Decision testing (Branch coverage): Percentage of decision outcomes exercised</div><h2>Cau hoi 19</h2><div class="qtext">Which statement is included in the common characteristics of experience-based test design techniques?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Test case can be derived systematically from these models [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Information about how the software is constructed is used to derive test cases</div><div class="opt correct">c. Knowledge about likely defects and their distribution is another source of information [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Model, either formal or informal, are used the specifications of the problems to be solved, the software or its component</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 4.1.2. A là định nghĩa ngắn gọn của black box test, Thêm D vào nữa là đủ câu trong sách, D là của Black box test. B là của white box test. chọn C</div><h2>Cau hoi 20</h2><div class="qtext">A defect was found during testing that the system crashed when the network got disconnected while receiving data the server. The defect was fixed by correcting codes which check the network availability during data transferring. The corresponding module did cover 100% of statement with existing test cases. To verify the fix and ensure more extensive coverage, some tests were designed and added to the test suite. What types of testing are NOT mentioned above?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Functional testing [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Structural testing</div><div class="opt ">c. Confirmation testing</div><div class="opt correct">d. Perfomance testing [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.3. ta dựa vào dấu hiệu "check the network availability" là của Functional testing, "To verify the fix " là của Confirmation testing, "100% of statement" là của Structural testing</div><h2>Cau hoi 21</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following options lists techniques categorized as White box design techniques?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Boundary Value analysis and Use Case Based testing [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Equivalence Partitioning and Decision Table testing</div><div class="opt ">c. Statement testing and Use Case Base testing</div><div class="opt correct">d. Decision coverage and Statement coverage [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 4.1.2</div><h2>Cau hoi 22</h2><div class="qtext">Which statement is included in the common characteristics of structure-based test design tecniques?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Test case can be derived systematically from these models [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Information about how the software is constructed is used to derive test cases [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Knowledge about likely defects and their distribution is another source of information</div><div class="opt ">d. Model, either formal or informal, are used the specifications of the problems to be solved, the software or its component</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 4.1.2</div><h2>Cau hoi 23</h2><div class="qtext">You are testing a scale system that determines shipping rates for a regional Web-based auto parts distributor. Identify how many equivalence classes are necessary for following range?</div><img src="data:image/png;base64," /><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. 4 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. 5</div><div class="opt ">c. 6</div><div class="opt correct">d. 7 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 24</h2><div class="qtext">Given the state diagram in Figure, which test case is the minimum series of valid transitions to cover every state?</div><img src="data:image/png;base64," /><div class="opt selectedright">a. SS-S1-S2-S4-S1-S3-ES [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. SS-S1-S2-S3-S4-ES</div><div class="opt ">c. SS-S1-S2-S4-S1-S3-S4-S1-S3-ES</div><div class="opt ">d. SS-S1-S4-S2-S1-S3-ES</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 25</h2><div class="qtext">How many test cases are need to achieve 100% statement coverage?</div><img src="data:image/png;base64," /><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. 5 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. 4</div><div class="opt correct">c. 2 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. 3</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 26</h2><div class="qtext">You have been give the following set of test case to run. You have been instructed to run them in order by risk and to accomplish the testing as quickly as possible to provide feedback to the developers as soon as possible. Give this information, what it the best order in which to run these tests ?</div><img src="data:image/png;base64," /><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. 5, 1,3,2,4 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. 1,2,4,3,5</div><div class="opt correct">c. 1,3,2,4,5 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. 3,4,5,1,2</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 27</h2><div class="qtext">You have received the following description section in an incident report. The report executed per the attached steps, but the data was incorrect. For example, the information in column 1 was wrong. See the attached screenshot. This report is critical to the users and they will be unable to do their jobs without this information. What is the biggest problem with this incident report?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. The developer won’t know how important the problem is [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. The developer won’t know how to repeat the test</div><div class="opt ">c. The developer won’t be able to see what the tester is saying is wrong</div><div class="opt correct">d. The developer doesn’t know what the tester expected to see [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 5.6 trong mô tả lỗi trên thiếu expected resutl</div><h2>Cau hoi 28</h2><div class="qtext">The activities and tasks performed by test leader depend on the project and product context, the people in the roles, and the organization. Which of following is NOT a task of the test leader?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Initiate the analysis, design, implementation, and execution of tests [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Monitor test results and check the status of exit criteria</div><div class="opt ">c. Contribute testing perspectives with other project activities</div><div class="opt correct">d. Set up test environment [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 5.1.2</div><h2>Cau hoi 29</h2><div class="qtext">Which of following terms is used to identified, version controlled, tracked for changes of all test items through the project and product life cycle?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Incident management [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Configuration management [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Test mornitoring</div><div class="opt ">d. Risk management</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 5.4 chú ý vào từ "the integrity"</div><h2>Cau hoi 30</h2><div class="qtext">Development staff may participate in testing especially at the lower levels, but the lack of objectivity often limits their effectiveness. The independent testers may have the authority to require and define the test processes and rules, but the testers should take on such process-related roles only in the presence of a clear management mandate to do so. Which of following is NOT drawbacks of independent testing?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Isolation from the development team [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Development team may be hard to find defects [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Independent testers may be seen as a bottleneck or blamed for delays in release</div><div class="opt ">d. Developers may lose a sense of responsibility for quality</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 5.1</div><h2>Cau hoi 31</h2><div class="qtext">Which of statement correctly describes about test monitoring and control?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Test monitoring: changing the test schedule due to availability and unavailability of test environment [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Test monitoring: re-prioriting test when an identified risk occur</div><div class="opt correct">c. Test control: guidance and the necessary corrective actions [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Test control: collects data from completed test activities</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 5.3. chú ý vào môi tả sai để loại trừ ta chọn đc C đúng. AB sai vì "changing the test schedule" "re-prioriting test" là của test control, D sai vì "assessing the effectiveness" là của test metrics nằm trong test report</div><h2>Cau hoi 32</h2><div class="qtext">Which of following is project risk?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. A problem with the development manager which is resulting in his rejecting all defect reports [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. An issue with the interface between the system under test and a peripheral device</div><div class="opt ">c. A failed performance test</div><div class="opt ">d. A module that performs incorrect calculations due to a defect in a formula</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 5.5</div><h2>Cau hoi 33</h2><div class="qtext">Which test activities are supported by test harness or unit test framework tools?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Test management and control. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Test specification and design</div><div class="opt correct">c. Test execution and logging [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Performance and monitoring</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 6.1</div><h2>Cau hoi 34</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following activities would a tester do during release planning?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Participate in the detailed risk analysis of user stories [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Help break down user stories into smaller and more detailed tasks</div><div class="opt ">c. Estimate testing tasks generated by new features planned for this iteration</div><div class="opt correct">d. Support the clarification of the user stories and ensure that they are testable [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 5.1.2. Chọn D là của Release plan, còn A B C là của Iteration plan</div><h2>Cau hoi 35</h2><div class="qtext">What is the most appropriate explanation of a user story?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. An artifact that the tester must review and sign off before testing can begin [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. An artifact used to detail only the functional requirements of the system</div><div class="opt ">c. An artifact documented by business representatives to help developers and testers understand the system requirements</div><div class="opt correct">d. An artifact written collaboratively by developers, testers, and business representatives to capture requirements [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.5.1. Chọn D vì đúng với sách tất cả các vị trí phải phối hợp hoặc hợp tác với nhau để viết US rõ ràng đầy đủ, Loại A vì sign off before testing- Tester phải ký cái này là ko có, Loại B vì detail only the functional- Chỉ viết detail cho functional ko là sai, cả functional và non-functional đều cần detail, Loại C vì nó nói US đc tạo bởi BA thì sai với tinh thần Agile.</div><h2>Cau hoi 36</h2><div class="qtext">Given the following user story: “An online application charges customers to ship purchased items, based on the following criteria: - Standard shipping costs for under 6 items - Shipping is $5 for 6-10 items - Shipping is free for more than 10 items Which of the following is the best black box test design technique for the user story?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. State Transition testing: Test the following states – browsing, logged in, selecting, purchasing, confirming, and exiting [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Decision tables: Test the following conditions – User logged in; At least 1 item in cart; Purchase confirmed; Funding approved; with the resulting action of – Ship Item</div><div class="opt correct">c. Boundary Value Analysis: Test the following inputs – 0, 5, 6, 10, 11, max [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Use Case Testing: Actor=customer; Prerequisites=customer logs in, selects and purchases items; Postconditions= items are shipped</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Với dữ liệu này thì chỉ có BVA là kỹ thuật phù hợp để design test case,</div><h2>Cau hoi 37</h2><div class="qtext">The User Story: “As a bank teller, I would like to be able to view all of my customer’s bank transactions on the screen, so I can answer his/her questions”. Which of the following can be considered as relevant acceptance test cases? i. Login as a bank teller, get the customer’s account balance for all open accounts ii. Login as a bank teller, enter a customer account ID, get his transactions history on the screen iii. Login as a bank teller, request customer account ID by using name abbreviations, and get his transaction history on the screen iv. Login as a bank teller, enter a customer IBAN (international bank account number), get his transaction history on the screen v. Login as a Bank Teller, enter a customer Account ID, get the Transactions history in less than 3 second on the screen</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. i, ii, iv [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. i, iii, iv</div><div class="opt ">c. ii, iv, v</div><div class="opt correct">d. ii, iii, iv [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 38</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following are examples of testable acceptance criteria for test related activities?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Structure based testing: White box testing in addition to black box testing is used [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt selectedright">b. System testing: At least 80% of functional regression tests are automated [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt correct">c. Security testing: A threat risk analysis scan is completed with no faults identified [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Performance testing: The application is responding in a reasonable amount of time with 5000 users</div><div class="opt ">e. Compatibility testing: The application is working on all major browsers</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.5 Các AC có khả năng test thì phải mô tả rõ ràng và cụ thể, ví dụ D loại vì ko rõ ràng " all major browsers" tất cả các trình duyệt là ko thể, C thì thiếu chưa quy định rõ về response time là bao nhiêu, A thì càng ko rõ ràng, nên chọn B, C</div><h2>Cau hoi 39</h2><div class="qtext">Given the following user story: “As the president, any data I upload should not be viewable by any other user of the system” During the first poker planning session, the following story points were given based on risk, effort, complexity, and proper extent of testing: Customers: 5 Developers: 5 Testers: 20 What is the best outcome following this planning session?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Because the customer’s and developer’s size estimates match, the team can be confident that this estimate is good and should move onto the next user story [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. The team should hold a conversation to understand why the testers felt this user story was significantly more work. Another round of the planning poker session should occur following that discussion [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Because the customer owns the system in the end, the customers’ estimates should be taken as correct when there is a conflict</div><div class="opt ">d. The poker planning sessions should continue until all estimated story points are an exact match between customers, developers, and testers</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 5.1.4 Vì ước lượng theo poker planning nên đến khi nào đạt được sự đồng thuận đa số mới dừng lại vì thế kết quả ước lượng lần 1 khác nhau như thế kia thì Tester nên giải thích vì sao, và 1 vòng ước lượng nữa cần được thực hiện</div><h2>Cau hoi 40</h2><div class="qtext">What does the term ‘Test Pyramid’ refer to and illustrate situations for?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. The team’s testing workload increases from sprint to sprint [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. The backlog size, and thus the number of tests, decreases</div><div class="opt correct">c. The number of automated unit tests is higher than the number of automated tests for higher test levels [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. The number of automated tests in place increases from sprint to sprint</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 5.1.6. Ở mức càng thấp Bottom level thì automated tests phải nhiều hơn so với mức cao Top level</div></body></html>